      "side": 1,
      "message": "WDYT:\n\n```\nhalf angle;\nif (bool(useAtanWorkaround)) {\n   angle \u003d half(2 * atan(-coord.y, length(coord) - coord.x));\n} else {\n   angle \u003d (coord.x !\u003d 0) ? mix(half(atan(-coord.y, -coord.x)) :\n                            sign(coord.y) * -1.5707963267949;\n}\n```\n\n- The stacked ternary is hard to read so I removed it. (One side or the other will get eliminated regardless.)\n\n- I moved the negation onto the literal to make it free.\n\nIf we could use ES3 I would suggest maybe:\n\n```\n   angle \u003d mix(half(atan(-coord.y, -coord.x)),\n               sign(coord.y) * -1.5707963267949             \n               coord.x \u003d\u003d 0);\n```\nThis would guarantee that it is branchless. (A ternary probably will be anyway.) At any rate, I\u0027m not worried about the cost of a `sign` and a multiply; that\u0027s really cheap regardless.",
